# BROWSER-note.md - Substack Note Publishing Patterns

## SS 9. Create & Publish Note

🚨 "New post" button opens Notes composer (NOT "Create post" which opens article editor).

### Step 1 — Open Notes composer

```bash
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000)); var btns = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button')); var newPostBtn = btns.find(b => b.innerText.trim() === 'New post' || b.innerText.trim() === \"What's on your mind?\"); if (!newPostBtn) return { error: 'New post button not found' }; newPostBtn.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true, cancelable: true })); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000)); var editor = document.querySelector('div[contenteditable=\"true\"]'); return { opened: !!editor }; }"}
ENDJSON
```

### Step 2 — Type note content and post

Uses `div[contenteditable="true"]` with paste approach. Post button disabled until content typed.

```bash
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000)); var editor = document.querySelector('div[contenteditable=\"true\"]'); if (!editor) return { error: 'no editor' }; var text = window.__data.text; editor.focus(); editor.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true })); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 300)); document.execCommand('selectAll'); document.execCommand('delete'); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 300)); var dt = new DataTransfer(); dt.setData('text/plain', text); editor.dispatchEvent(new ClipboardEvent('paste', { clipboardData: dt, bubbles: true, cancelable: true })); if (!editor.innerText.trim()) { document.execCommand('insertText', false, text); } editor.dispatchEvent(new InputEvent('input', { bubbles: true, inputType: 'insertText' })); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000)); var btns = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button')); var postBtn = btns.find(function(b) { return b.innerText.trim() === 'Post' && !b.disabled; }); if (!postBtn) return { typed: true, len: editor.innerText.length, error: 'Post button disabled' }; postBtn.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('click', { bubbles: true, cancelable: true })); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 3000)); var editorGone = !document.querySelector('div[contenteditable=\"true\"]'); return { typed: true, submitted: true, editorClosed: editorGone }; }", "data": {"text": "YOUR_NOTE_HERE"}}
ENDJSON
```

Note content: 50–120 words (per content-writer §8); content comes from `config.content_source`, never drafted here. NO hashtags.

