## SS 9b. Attach Image to Note

🚨 **Pre-conditions:** (1) PNG exists at a filesystem path; (2) **composer MUST be open** — the hidden `<input type="file">` only exists in the DOM when the Notes composer is mounted. HEARTBEAT publish_note runs this AFTER Step 2 (type + post preparation) to match.

Direct-set on hidden file input via the upload endpoint's `selector` mode (no button click needed — setting files fires the input's `change` event and the image attaches, showing a blob preview):

```bash
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/upload -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d "{\"filePath\":\"${PNG}\",\"selector\":\"input[type=\\\"file\\\"][accept*=\\\"image\\\"]\",\"timeoutMs\":10000}"
```

Expected result: `{"ok":true, ...}`. If the selector doesn't match (no composer / no file input) → the endpoint errors; agent logs and falls back to text-only.

**Verify image attached:**

```bash
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1500)); var dialog = document.querySelector('[role=\"dialog\"]') || document.body; var blobImg = Array.from(dialog.querySelectorAll('img')).find(function(i) { return (i.src || '').startsWith('blob:'); }); return { attached: !!blobImg }; }"}
ENDJSON
```

If `attached: false` → return error to HEARTBEAT; fall back to text-only.
